WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.233
The rebuilding of Lumiose City continues

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.966
as our heroes are thinking about what their futures hold,

3
00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.700
and of course, that includes Serena.

4
00:00:22.066 --> 00:00:23.666
- All right.
- Huh?

5
00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.966
Keep on your journey to your heart's content.

6
00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:31.000
Once you're all ready for the next step, you just give me a call.

7
00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:36.933
- Huh? Hey, look at that.
- Huh?

8
00:00:37.566 --> 00:00:40.566
The light of hope even illuminated Prism Tower.

9
00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:45.433
There are still many wounds in Lumiose City,

10
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.966
but this light will guide us as we continue our recovery.

11
00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:53.233
You know, lighting up Prism Tower was great. Everybody loved it.

12
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.933
All those smiles.

13
00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:56.466
Dedenne.

14
00:00:56.966 --> 00:00:57.933
It was great.

15
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.866
One of our first big steps to recovery.

16
00:01:03.666 --> 00:01:04.666
Oh.

17
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.833
- Oh, I see.
- What do you think?

18
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.533
Hmm. I think it's a great idea.

19
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.966
Okay, I'll be glad to help out.

20
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:16.666
Thank you so much.

21
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.200
Braixen.

22
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.300
♪ I stand tall 'cause I know I'm a winner ♪

23
00:01:28.933 --> 00:01:31.966
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

24
00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.600
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

25
00:01:35.666 --> 00:01:37.200
♪ Pokémon ♪

26
00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:39.233
♪ Pokémon ♪

27
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.366
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

28
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.633
♪ I stand tall 'cause I know I'm a winner ♪

29
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.900
♪ Pokémon ♪

30
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.866
♪ Pokémon ♪

31
00:01:46.933 --> 00:01:48.233
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

32
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.033
Where are we going, Serena?

33
00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:06.266
You'll know when we get there.

34
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:07.400
- Huh?
- Pika?

35
00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:15.033
Wow.

36
00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.633
- What's up?
- So many people.

37
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.600
- Everyone.
- Huh?

38
00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:20.933
Professor Sycamore.

39
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:25.400
- Something going on here?
- There's a performance exhibition today.

40
00:02:25.533 --> 00:02:26.600
Huh?

41
00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:29.266
- It was Serena's idea.
- Serena?

42
00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:33.000
Mm-hm. This is what I love. It's what I wanna do.

43
00:02:33.733 --> 00:02:37.766
Serena has really inspired me. I wanna help out however I can.

44
00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:41.533
As a Pokémon Showcase finalist, what do you think?

45
00:02:42.666 --> 00:02:43.866
I hope you approve.

46
00:02:44.966 --> 00:02:46.800
- Yeah.
- Serena!

47
00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.733
- Huh?
- Pika?

48
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.166
- I'm finally here.
- Shauna.

49
00:02:51.233 --> 00:02:53.266
Sorry. I know it was last minute.

50
00:02:53.733 --> 00:02:56.133
No prob. I just wanna help you out.

51
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.033
We wanna help out, too.

52
00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.566
- Tell us what you need.
- Trevor's right.

53
00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.200
- Trevor! Tierno!
- Sawyer!

54
00:03:03.666 --> 00:03:05.733
It's so nice to meet up like this.

55
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:08.800
Watching on TV, we were so worried about you.

56
00:03:09.266 --> 00:03:12.400
Thanks, guys. But see? We're all doing fine.

57
00:03:12.466 --> 00:03:13.300
Pika, pika.

58
00:03:13.766 --> 00:03:16.800
- Great.
- We're happy to see everyone in one piece.

59
00:03:17.266 --> 00:03:20.900
So, let's get this show on the road. What do you say?

60
00:03:21.233 --> 00:03:22.066
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

61
00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:27.366
Ladies and gentlemen,

62
00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:32.400
presenting, as a special treat, our very own Pokémon Showcase performance.

63
00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:35.000
It's marvelous!

64
00:03:44.166 --> 00:03:46.600
- We hope you enjoy the show.
- Braixen!

65
00:03:46.666 --> 00:03:48.433
- Yeah!
- All right!

66
00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.366
Braixen, Flamethrower.

67
00:03:51.366 --> 00:03:53.900
Ivysaur, Solar Beam!

68
00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.366
Braixen!

69
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.533
- Look at that.
- Awesome.

70
00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.800
Say, I know those girls.

71
00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:05.300
They both competed in the Master Class.

72
00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.433
That was so beautiful.

73
00:04:18.633 --> 00:04:20.000
- Pika, pi!
- Huh?

74
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.500
- Alain and Mairin are here, too.
- Hi.

75
00:04:23.766 --> 00:04:27.566
I've never seen Serena perform before. She's great, isn't she?

76
00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:28.566
Pancham!

77
00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.600
A Pokémon Showcase here? That is a puzzler, isn't it?

78
00:04:35.766 --> 00:04:37.200
These are twerps.

79
00:04:37.266 --> 00:04:39.900
- Wobbuffet!
- Inkay! Inkay!

80
00:04:40.366 --> 00:04:42.233
And distracted twerps, as well.

81
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.500
An excellent chance to grab Pikachu.

82
00:04:44.666 --> 00:04:45.800
Don't you agree?

83
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.033
Aah! Well, I've seen enough!

84
00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:53.333
Gourgeist.

85
00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.566
I'll show them a real performance.

86
00:04:55.633 --> 00:04:58.866
- Now, Gourgeist, let's educate them.
- Gour.

87
00:04:59.333 --> 00:05:01.133
And liftoff.

88
00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:02.966
No putting out that fire.

89
00:05:03.233 --> 00:05:04.666
Wobbu, wobbu.

90
00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.000
Now, follow the bouncing me.

91
00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:12.733
Gourgeist, Seed Bomb!

92
00:05:13.033 --> 00:05:14.200
Gour-gour-gour-geist!

93
00:05:14.766 --> 00:05:17.600
- That's Jessilee!
- She's great. I'm a big fan.

94
00:05:17.666 --> 00:05:20.233
It's everyone from the Master Class finals!

95
00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.600
- It's Jessilee.
- Wow, she came!

96
00:05:24.066 --> 00:05:26.966
Sure. Where there's a stage, there's Jessilee.

97
00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:29.466
All together now.

98
00:05:29.933 --> 00:05:31.233
It's showtime!

99
00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.533
Sylveon, use Swift!

100
00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.533
Veon!

101
00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.666
Flabébé, Moonblast!

102
00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.100
- Oh, yeah.
- This is so cool.

103
00:06:10.266 --> 00:06:13.233
Hey, Alain, why don't we have a dance, too?

104
00:06:13.533 --> 00:06:15.266
Uh, I don't think I should.

105
00:06:15.333 --> 00:06:17.566
- Come on. Let's dance.
- Chespin!

106
00:06:19.433 --> 00:06:22.566
You need to have some fun. Yeah, go on.

107
00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:23.866
Professor.

108
00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.833
See, Alain? It's really a lot of fun.

109
00:06:29.466 --> 00:06:30.766
Che!

110
00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:37.266
- Professor, let's dance.
- Dedenne!

111
00:06:37.333 --> 00:06:39.200
Who, me? Uh...

112
00:06:39.266 --> 00:06:41.533
Lovely, this feeling I have.

113
00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.366
It's like I've found my true calling.

114
00:06:44.733 --> 00:06:50.066
Perhaps I should remain here after all and aim for the title of Kalos Queen.

115
00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.866
Don't forget your day job, Your Highness.

116
00:07:00.733 --> 00:07:06.033
- They're so happy. Don't you think?
- Yeah. I'm so glad everyone's having fun.

117
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.633
That's all!

118
00:07:32.166 --> 00:07:33.933
- Yeah!
- Great! Woo-hoo!

119
00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.466
- Amazing!
- Yeah!

120
00:07:35.533 --> 00:07:37.300
- Serena?

121
00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.500
Huh?

122
00:07:40.733 --> 00:07:41.700
Wow, Mom.

123
00:07:45.366 --> 00:07:47.266
Thank you for helping my daughter.

124
00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.400
My pleasure. She's a big help.

125
00:07:49.466 --> 00:07:52.466
The way she's been taking care of my boy and girl,

126
00:07:52.533 --> 00:07:56.933
- Serena's so important to all of us.
- I'm so glad she's been helping out.

127
00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.866
Mom, why not go and relax for a while? I'll make some dinner.

128
00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.866
You'll make it?

129
00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:07.733
That's right. You might not believe it, but I've turned into quite a good cook.

130
00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.133
Pika?

131
00:08:09.666 --> 00:08:11.966
- Chespin.
- I'll help you out, too.

132
00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:14.733
- Pikachu.
- Tell us what to do and it's done.

133
00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.366
All right, Clemont. You take in the bread.

134
00:08:17.833 --> 00:08:20.266
- Sure.
- Ash, you grab the veggies.

135
00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:22.366
- Got it.
- I wanna help, too.

136
00:08:23.166 --> 00:08:27.166
So, Grace, Serena's performance, did you get a chance to see it today?

137
00:08:27.233 --> 00:08:28.133
Yes.

138
00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:32.166
Uh, I've been worried about how my daughter's been doing,

139
00:08:32.233 --> 00:08:35.400
but I guess there was no reason. It was wonderful.

140
00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.533
And it was all Serena's idea.

141
00:08:38.466 --> 00:08:39.466
Her idea?

142
00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.333
You have a wonderful daughter.

143
00:08:42.733 --> 00:08:44.200
Just wonderful.

144
00:08:46.933 --> 00:08:49.166
Thank you. You're very kind.

145
00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:58.600
- I'll be heading back to the hotel.
- Wait. Mom?

146
00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.800
Can I--? Can I stay with you at the hotel tonight?

147
00:09:18.233 --> 00:09:21.366
Serena, is there something you'd like to talk about?

148
00:09:21.433 --> 00:09:22.400
Huh?

149
00:09:22.766 --> 00:09:25.866
Staying in a hotel with me is not your usual style.

150
00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.900
What's on your mind? I'm all ears.

151
00:09:30.433 --> 00:09:31.366
See, Mom...

152
00:09:33.633 --> 00:09:35.433
today, on stage...

153
00:09:36.166 --> 00:09:39.933
I finally realized why I truly love performing.

154
00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:45.233
And I understand a little better what I was missing before.

155
00:09:47.766 --> 00:09:53.066
Looking at all the smiles in the crowd... and how happy they all looked...

156
00:09:53.533 --> 00:09:58.400
made me realize what I really want is to make even more people smile, like Aria.

157
00:10:00.233 --> 00:10:04.666
But if I do that, I'm afraid I'll lose what I gained on my journey.

158
00:10:06.266 --> 00:10:11.066
Well, I don't agree with that. Is that all your journey meant to you?

159
00:10:11.933 --> 00:10:13.833
I can see that you've changed.

160
00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:17.866
But your experiences, they're always going to be a part of you.

161
00:10:18.733 --> 00:10:20.500
Have more confidence.

162
00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.066
Mama.

163
00:10:24.966 --> 00:10:27.600
Don't forget you're your mother's daughter.

164
00:10:31.366 --> 00:10:35.400
Okay, let's get some sleep. We've got an early day tomorrow.

165
00:10:38.566 --> 00:10:40.166
Are you leaving already?

166
00:10:40.333 --> 00:10:41.800
You should stay longer.

167
00:10:42.233 --> 00:10:45.366
Serena's doing fine. That's what's important.

168
00:10:45.833 --> 00:10:46.700
Thanks, Mom.

169
00:10:47.433 --> 00:10:49.300
Let me know once you've decided

170
00:10:49.366 --> 00:10:51.366
- what we talked about.
- Okay.

171
00:10:52.666 --> 00:10:56.600
All right, gang, come visit me whenever you're in Vaniville Town.

172
00:10:56.733 --> 00:10:58.366
The door's always unlocked.

173
00:10:58.866 --> 00:10:59.733
Pika, pika!
Great!

174
00:11:00.766 --> 00:11:02.200
Yippee, yay!

175
00:11:03.233 --> 00:11:04.300
Bye, Serena.

176
00:11:08.466 --> 00:11:12.266
So, should we all head over to Professor Sycamore's lab?

177
00:11:12.333 --> 00:11:15.566
Nope. I'm gonna work on my new dance with Serena.

178
00:11:16.766 --> 00:11:18.066
You promised.

179
00:11:18.533 --> 00:11:21.300
Since all the wild Pokémon left Lumiose City,

180
00:11:21.366 --> 00:11:25.333
we've been asked to help out. We've got a big job ahead of us.

181
00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:29.800
- Awesome. You'll do great.
- Well, then, we'll be heading out, too.

182
00:11:29.866 --> 00:11:32.500
- Take care of yourselves, everyone.
- Ow! Aah!

183
00:11:32.566 --> 00:11:35.033
Okay, okay. My ear's gonna fall off.

184
00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.866
All right, I need to go as well.

185
00:11:37.933 --> 00:11:40.200
So, what's next? Where are you going?

186
00:11:41.066 --> 00:11:45.100
To what's left of Lysandre's offices. Steven asked me to help out.

187
00:11:46.666 --> 00:11:50.733
It seems the Giant Rock has disappeared before and then reappeared.

188
00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:56.133
He believes the Giant Rock may not have completely disappeared this time either.

189
00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.266
That's what he's working on now.

190
00:11:58.766 --> 00:12:03.900
See, I got this Key Stone from Steven. Maybe we can be of some use to him.

191
00:12:05.033 --> 00:12:08.300
- I'd like to pay him back for his help.
- Sounds great.

192
00:12:08.533 --> 00:12:12.866
Ash... next time we meet, let's battle, okay?

193
00:12:13.266 --> 00:12:16.033
In the meantime, I'll keep gaining experience.

194
00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.666
Sure. It's a deal.

195
00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:21.600
- I'm winning next time.
- Yeah? So am I.

196
00:12:24.933 --> 00:12:26.500
- See you.
- Bye-bye.

197
00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:27.966
See you soon.

198
00:12:28.033 --> 00:12:29.933
- Take care of yourself.
- Right.

199
00:12:36.966 --> 00:12:39.633
I should be heading back to the Lumiose Gym.

200
00:12:39.866 --> 00:12:43.333
- I've still got more cleaning up to do.
- I wanna help.

201
00:12:43.666 --> 00:12:45.733
- Dedenne.
- What about you?

202
00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.300
Yeah, what should I do?

203
00:12:47.766 --> 00:12:49.100
What are you gonna do?

204
00:12:49.166 --> 00:12:52.566
- Me? I don't know.
- You can stay with me, you know.

205
00:12:52.633 --> 00:12:53.733
Huh?

206
00:12:55.633 --> 00:12:57.733
Who's that Pokémon?

207
00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.466
- It's Hoppip.
- Hoppip.

208
00:13:10.133 --> 00:13:12.166
No way. All right!

209
00:13:12.333 --> 00:13:14.833
They say they're gonna reopen the airport soon.

210
00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.100
Pika, pika.

211
00:13:26.333 --> 00:13:29.700
Look at that. Lumiose City is almost back to normal.

212
00:13:29.766 --> 00:13:30.600
Yeah.

213
00:13:35.066 --> 00:13:36.900
Whoa. Serena, check it out.

214
00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:39.600
So cute.

215
00:13:42.433 --> 00:13:43.400
Huh?

216
00:13:50.833 --> 00:13:52.133
Pikachu.

217
00:13:52.533 --> 00:13:54.600
Pi-pika.

218
00:13:55.466 --> 00:13:56.700
Man, this is good.

219
00:13:56.766 --> 00:13:59.133
Lumiose's famous foods are back, too.

220
00:13:59.233 --> 00:14:00.133
- Hmm
- Pika?

221
00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:03.433
Serena?

222
00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:04.766
Huh?

223
00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:07.866
- What?
- Let's have a battle.

224
00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.433
- Pika!
- Now?

225
00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:13.433
Wait.

226
00:14:13.966 --> 00:14:15.433
- Come on, this way.
- Ash!

227
00:14:19.966 --> 00:14:21.066
I remember this.

228
00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:25.900
When I first came to Lumiose City, I battled with Clemont right here.

229
00:14:26.166 --> 00:14:27.266
Pika, pika.

230
00:14:27.333 --> 00:14:29.166
Right here? What do you know?

231
00:14:29.633 --> 00:14:31.600
That was a really long time ago.

232
00:14:32.433 --> 00:14:36.833
Thing is, when I'm worried, having a Pokémon battle always helps.

233
00:14:37.033 --> 00:14:38.900
- Makes me feel great.
- Huh?

234
00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:44.133
- You'll feel better fast.
- Pikachu.

235
00:14:44.366 --> 00:14:45.566
Maybe you're right.

236
00:14:45.633 --> 00:14:49.233
Know what? I've never had a proper battle with you before.

237
00:14:51.233 --> 00:14:52.966
Okay, let's do it.

238
00:14:53.033 --> 00:14:54.233
Awesome!

239
00:14:58.533 --> 00:15:01.266
Now, Braixen, let's go!

240
00:15:03.466 --> 00:15:05.800
Braixen!

241
00:15:06.433 --> 00:15:07.933
Going with Braixen, huh?

242
00:15:08.266 --> 00:15:09.466
You're up, Pikachu.

243
00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:11.966
Pikachu!

244
00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:22.733
- Okay, Pikachu, use Quick Attack!
- Pika! Pi, pi, pi, pi, pi, pi.

245
00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.533
Braixen!

246
00:15:26.233 --> 00:15:28.366
- Oh, no, Braixen!
- Braixen.

247
00:15:28.966 --> 00:15:30.133
Pikachu's so fast.

248
00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:33.366
- Let's keep it up. Iron Tail, let's go!
- Pika!

249
00:15:34.066 --> 00:15:35.266
Chu!

250
00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:38.500
- Defense!
- Pika!

251
00:15:41.066 --> 00:15:42.933
Chu, pika!

252
00:15:44.833 --> 00:15:45.733
Braixen!

253
00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.100
Braix.

254
00:15:49.433 --> 00:15:50.566
I know what to do.

255
00:15:50.633 --> 00:15:53.233
- Just act like we're rehearsing.
- Braixen.

256
00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:55.900
All right, Flamethrower!

257
00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.300
- Braixen!
- Dodge it, quick!

258
00:15:58.366 --> 00:15:59.266
Pika!

259
00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:01.366
- Jump up!
- Braixen.

260
00:16:01.966 --> 00:16:04.633
Braixen!

261
00:16:05.633 --> 00:16:08.700
- Braixen, use Scratch!
- Braixen!

262
00:16:09.166 --> 00:16:10.300
Iron Tail, go!

263
00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.666
Braixen, use Fire Blast!

264
00:16:16.433 --> 00:16:17.566
Pikachu!

265
00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.733
- Yeah. All right!
- Braixen.

266
00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:22.466
Pikachu.

267
00:16:23.433 --> 00:16:24.533
Pikachu.

268
00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:27.966
Way to go, Serena. You and Braixen make an awesome team.

269
00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:29.733
Thanks.

270
00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:32.533
Your Pokémon are strong. All of them.

271
00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:35.500
Braixen and Pancham, and don't forget Sylveon.

272
00:16:35.566 --> 00:16:36.500
Huh?

273
00:16:37.066 --> 00:16:41.333
Of course I know. Greninja and I had our share of problems for a while.

274
00:16:41.466 --> 00:16:45.000
Then I figured it out. You can't do anything by yourself.

275
00:16:45.066 --> 00:16:49.233
When you're with Pokémon who support you, it makes you do your best.

276
00:16:49.333 --> 00:16:50.200
Oh, Ash.

277
00:16:50.666 --> 00:16:53.866
I'll tell you one thing. I'll always be cheering you on and on.

278
00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:55.466
Pika!

279
00:16:55.533 --> 00:16:58.266
Oh, Ash, Pikachu, thank you.

280
00:17:03.666 --> 00:17:04.866
- Pancham.
- Veon.

281
00:17:05.333 --> 00:17:08.233
I'm really not alone. You're all with me.

282
00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.833
- Braixen.
- Cham-cham.

283
00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:11.733
On.

284
00:17:12.266 --> 00:17:14.833
Braixen, Pancham, Sylveon,

285
00:17:15.066 --> 00:17:19.099
I know it may not be an easy journey, but will you take it with me?

286
00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.599
- Cham.
- Braixen.

287
00:17:21.666 --> 00:17:22.599
On.

288
00:17:23.066 --> 00:17:24.733
Thanks so much, all of you.

289
00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:29.400
Ash, I know what I wanna do.

290
00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.700
So, we meet again.

291
00:17:35.533 --> 00:17:38.800
I've been waiting. Have you found an answer yet?

292
00:17:39.266 --> 00:17:43.466
- Yes, ma'am. I sure have.
- All right. What is it?

293
00:17:49.066 --> 00:17:52.466
Forgive me, ma'am, but I can't go with you.

294
00:17:54.333 --> 00:17:55.166
Hmm.

295
00:17:56.033 --> 00:18:00.733
Aria helped me. She taught me that my smile can give other people strength.

296
00:18:01.366 --> 00:18:03.700
I experienced that for the first time.

297
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:09.833
Even though they'd been through so much, people smiled watching my performance.

298
00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:14.700
That's what made me decide. I want lots of different people to see me perform.

299
00:18:15.166 --> 00:18:17.733
That's what I have to do to really grow.

300
00:18:17.966 --> 00:18:21.433
If I were to study with you, I'd depend on you too much.

301
00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.933
That's not what I need.

302
00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:25.633
You see? They're my friends.

303
00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:28.300
I wanna see lots of places with my Pokémon.

304
00:18:28.466 --> 00:18:29.600
Other regions.

305
00:18:29.666 --> 00:18:32.166
I'm certain we'll experience things together

306
00:18:32.233 --> 00:18:34.633
that will help us to grow and mature.

307
00:18:34.833 --> 00:18:36.600
- Braixen.
- Pancham.

308
00:18:36.666 --> 00:18:37.533
Veon.

309
00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:41.200
It's probably not what you expected, but I made my decision.

310
00:18:42.566 --> 00:18:45.800
Well, that's a shame. I want the best for you, too.

311
00:18:46.333 --> 00:18:50.400
You're the first person to ever turn down an offer of help from me.

312
00:18:52.766 --> 00:18:54.766
Have you decided where you'll go?

313
00:18:55.633 --> 00:18:57.400
Uh, no, not yet.

314
00:18:58.466 --> 00:19:01.966
- Well, how about the Hoenn region?
- Hoenn?

315
00:19:02.466 --> 00:19:06.666
There they have Pokémon contests, which are different than showcases.

316
00:19:06.733 --> 00:19:11.600
Pokémon contests would be just the thing. A great way to gain good experience.

317
00:19:12.633 --> 00:19:14.633
Great. I'll do it.

318
00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:15.966
Very good.

319
00:19:16.066 --> 00:19:20.333
When you return, show me everything you learned while you were there.

320
00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.333
I'm looking forward to seeing all the ways you'll grow.

321
00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:24.833
Hmm.

322
00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:26.466
Didn't I tell you?

323
00:19:26.933 --> 00:19:29.833
My dear, I'm a big fan of yours.

324
00:19:31.966 --> 00:19:34.333
Thanks. I promise I'll come back.

325
00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.200
Ta-da!

326
00:19:46.433 --> 00:19:48.066
Attention, please!

327
00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:52.366
All right, I've decided I'm going to go on a performance-training journey.

328
00:19:52.433 --> 00:19:54.933
- Huh?
- You're gonna leave us, too?

329
00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:55.933
Den-enne.

330
00:19:57.866 --> 00:20:02.600
Yeah. I realize I need to learn a lot in order to grow as a Pokémon performer,

331
00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.000
so I've gotta go.

332
00:20:04.233 --> 00:20:06.400
There are so many places to see.

333
00:20:06.866 --> 00:20:10.166
The Hoenn region is a great place for Pokémon contests,

334
00:20:10.233 --> 00:20:11.800
so I'm going there first.

335
00:20:13.066 --> 00:20:15.133
That's great. Good for you.

336
00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:16.666
Thanks, Ash.

337
00:20:16.733 --> 00:20:20.200
I'm not sure where it will lead me, but I'll do my best.

338
00:20:20.633 --> 00:20:22.000
We'll do our best.

339
00:20:22.066 --> 00:20:23.133
- Braixen.
- Pancham.

340
00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:27.866
Who knows? Maybe we can help lots of other people find their dreams.

341
00:20:28.633 --> 00:20:31.600
I think-- No, I'm sure I can do that.

342
00:20:32.066 --> 00:20:33.566
Yeah. Go for it.

343
00:20:34.033 --> 00:20:34.866
Pika, pika!

344
00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.566
Following a Pokémon battle with Ash,

345
00:20:37.633 --> 00:20:40.266
Serena's decided what path she will follow.

346
00:20:40.333 --> 00:20:43.533
And so, the day when Ash, Clemont, and Bonnie set off

347
00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:47.800
to find their own futures is coming soon, as the journey continues.
